cificity MAP kinase phosphatase, negatively regulates Slt2p MAP kinase by direct dephosphorylation, diffuse localization under normal conditions shifts to punctate localization after heat shock	None	None	Plasma membrane H+-ATPase, pumps protons out of the cell; major regulator of cytoplasmic pH and plasma membrane potential; part of the P2 subgroup of cation-transporting ATPases	Putative serine/threonine protein kinase; involved in the adaptation to low concentrations of glucose independent of the SNF3 regulated pathway	Vacuolar Ca2+ ATPase involved in depleting cytosol of Ca2+ ions; prevents growth inhibition by activation of calcineurin in the presence of elevated concentrations of calcium; similar to mammalian PMCA1a	Subunit of the RecQ (Sgs1p) - Topo III (Top3p) complex; stimulates superhelical relaxing and ssDNA binding activities of Top3p; involved in response to DNA damage; null mutants display increased rates of recombination and delayed S phase	Protein of unknown function, involved in invasive and pseudohyphal growth	Threonine aldolase, catalyzes the cleavage of L-allo-threonine and L-threonine to glycine; involved in glycine biosynthesis	Protein of unknown function, involved in proteasome-dependent catabolite inactivation of fructose-1,6-bisphosphatase; contains LisH and CTLH domains, like Vid30p; dosage-dependent regulator of START	Small heat shock protein (sHSP) with chaperone activity; forms barrel-shaped oligomers that suppress unfolded protein aggregation; involved in cytoskeleton reorganization after heat shock	DNA damage-responsive protein, expression is increased in response to heat-shock stress or treatments that produce DNA lesions; contains multiple repeats of the amino acid sequence NNNDSYGS	Multistress response protein, expression is activated by a variety of xenobiotic agents and environmental or physiological stresses	Protein that functions with Nca2p to regulate mitochondrial expression of subunits 6 (Atp6p) and 8 (Atp8p ) of the Fo-F1 ATP 